  "question": {
    "text": "A metal bar <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> can slide on two parallel thick metallic rails separated by a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>. A resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> and an inductance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> are connected to the rails as shown in the figure. A long straight wire, carrying a constant current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> is placed in the plane of the rails as shown. The bar <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> is held at rest at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> from the long wire. At&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, it is made to slide on the rails away from the wire.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" height=\"157\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0009092_Ques1_1.jpg\" width=\"185\" /><br />\r<br />\r&nbsp;It is observed that at time<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></math>, the metal bar <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> is at a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> from the long wire and the resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> carries a current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. The net charge that has flown through resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></math> is",
